(5300919, 771367, 97166, '<td valign="top">She stood there and looked into that place, and remembered a time when the world seemed a little more magical.  Less filled with worry and care. A time when wonder and beauty and imagination ruled.<br/> <br/>She stood there and closed her eyes and listened to the music of the water as it played its forever song, and her mind took her back to a time when that music wasn''t just a sound, but a concert being played by the fairy folk that she had so fully believed in.  Not just water, but a symphony of ethereal strings on instruments plucked by the gossamer fingers of peoples living only just on this side of reality.<br/> <br/>She stood there and smiled a sad little smile, and opened her eyes, and the concert became mere water once again, the fairy folk flitted away and became the falling leaves, the world returned in stark and unforgiving clarity, and the inner child that had returned to her so briefly ran off with a laughter that drifted away on the breeze.<br/> <br/>Then she turned and walked off to her adulthood.</td>', 'She stood there and looked into that place, and remembered a time when the world seemed a little more magical.  Less filled with worry and care. A time when wonder and beauty and imagination ruled. She stood there and closed her eyes and listened to the music of the water as it played its forever song, and her mind took her back to a time when that music wasn''t just a sound, but a concert being played by the fairy folk that she had so fully believed in.  Not just water, but a symphony of ethereal strings on instruments plucked by the gossamer fingers of peoples living only just on this side of reality. She stood there and smiled a sad little smile, and opened her eyes, and the concert became mere water once again, the fairy folk flitted away and became the falling leaves, the world returned in stark and unforgiving clarity, and the inner child that had returned to her so briefly ran off with a laughter that drifted away on the breeze. Then she turned and walked off to her adulthood.', '2009-03-11 00:54:56.000000', NULL, 1),
