(5313578, 771858, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier now coming back to leave comments. A synchronized flight of the red, white and blues! I do like the widescreen version a bit better for you get a sense of the wide open sky that these fabulous flyers occupy. It gives us/me a better sense of being there at this airshow by allowing us to project into the scene as one of the spectators. Oh don''t get me wrong the other version that remember seeing in the portfolio was a fabulous shot as well. But if I remember correctly it was a tight square crop that gave a tight narrow ''tunnel vision view'' that does not readily allow one to project themselves as there at the event. Great action, colors and sense of ''being there'' to ''witness'' this amazing sight. Great job!</td>', 'Voted earlier now coming back to leave comments. A synchronized flight of the red, white and blues! I do like the widescreen version a bit better for you get a sense of the wide open sky that these fabulous flyers occupy. It gives us/me a better sense of being there at this airshow by allowing us to project into the scene as one of the spectators. Oh don''t get me wrong the other version that remember seeing in the portfolio was a fabulous shot as well. But if I remember correctly it was a tight square crop that gave a tight narrow ''tunnel vision view'' that does not readily allow one to project themselves as there at the event. Great action, colors and sense of ''being there'' to ''witness'' this amazing sight. Great job!', '2009-03-11 19:42:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5313579, 771919, 37845, '<td valign="top">I''d say. That bug looks like it is in its own personal paradise.</td>', 'I''d say. That bug looks like it is in its own personal paradise.', '2009-03-11 19:42:37.000000', NULL, 1),
