(5319936, 770508, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to leave comments. A study in shapes and blended hues is what I see as appealing in this composition. All are portals or windows that give us an outside view but not all are the same shape and this is an exploration of them. To find so many on one wall in this arrangement is most unusual. You have circles, squares, and then the dark rectangle that contains both shapes. Heh, interestingly enough you could make the observation that your photo itself is another ''portal'' that we are looking out of to see this arrangement of windows. We are looking through your rectangular portal to see these ''window''s on the wall opposite. The state of the colors on the wall itself a ''whitewashed'' or ''watercolor'' look gives it the appearance of a painting. We can see the places where the white brushstrokes has left the canvas such that we see the grey underneath.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to leave comments. A study in shapes and blended hues is what I see as appealing in this composition. All are portals or windows that give us an outside view but not all are the same shape and this is an exploration of them. To find so many on one wall in this arrangement is most unusual. You have circles, squares, and then the dark rectangle that contains both shapes. Heh, interestingly enough you could make the observation that your photo itself is another ''portal'' that we are looking out of to see this arrangement of windows. We are looking through your rectangular portal to see these ''window''s on the wall opposite. The state of the colors on the wall itself a ''whitewashed'' or ''watercolor'' look gives it the appearance of a painting. We can see the places where the white brushstrokes has left the canvas such that we see the grey underneath.', '2009-03-12 09:33:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5319937, 770655, 83845, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Well done!</td>', 'Very nice!  Well done!', '2009-03-12 09:33:53.000000', NULL, 1),
