(5323067, 772265, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment....<b>and left a long comment earlier but don''t know why it left just a ''C''. So typing out my comment again! </b> <br/> <br/>Wow! Absolutely love this great action shot and from an angle we don''t normally get to see too! Love the look of concentration on his face as he is focusing all his energy on *SMASHING* that birdie into next week! The overhead angle really allows us to appreciate the expression on his face. It also shows us what looks like his body is contorted with the position of his feet but upon further study we see that he has LEAPT up into the air. The leap, the position of his hands, and the concentration all show the power of the blow he is about to deliver when he hits that birdie. Color and clarity are wonderful. Some areas are not in such sharp focus such as the racket and the birdie but that is fine because it shows us a sense of motion. This is a great sports action capture! Good job!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment....and left a long comment earlier but don''t know why it left just a ''C''. So typing out my comment again!   Wow! Absolutely love this great action shot and from an angle we don''t normally get to see too! Love the look of concentration on his face as he is focusing all his energy on *SMASHING* that birdie into next week! The overhead angle really allows us to appreciate the expression on his face. It also shows us what looks like his body is contorted with the position of his feet but upon further study we see that he has LEAPT up into the air. The leap, the position of his hands, and the concentration all show the power of the blow he is about to deliver when he hits that birdie. Color and clarity are wonderful. Some areas are not in such sharp focus such as the racket and the birdie but that is fine because it shows us a sense of motion. This is a great sports action capture! Good job!', '2009-03-12 13:20:19.000000', NULL, 1),
