(5323636, 771932, 3102, '<td valign="top">Hello there!<br/> <br/>I have tried to make a habit out of leaving a super-extensive comment for "milestone" votes of mine.  Turns out, your shot is the 200,000th vote I have cast at DPC!  So... for what it''s worth, here is my super-extensive comment :)<br/> <br/>First, the positives.  I can see that you used a flash to brighten up the horse''s face.  That looks like it helped to bring out the detail in the fur a bit.  I wonder what a bigger source of light, like a reflector, would have done here.<br/> <br/>I like the various colors in here.  The greens stand out nicely behind the horse... and the puffy gray clouds add a touch of contrast to the white clouds in the sky.<br/> <br/>Overall I think the composition is good... I might have chopped out just a little more of the sky, though.<br/> <br/>As for nitpicky things... I probably would have cloned out the tiny little bird above his back -- it looks like a dust speck (maybe it is a dust speck!).  I would have been tempted to clone out the hot sot on his forehead, too.<br/> <br/>I guess my biggest nitpick would be that it''s a little plain, and maybe it doesn''t really "tell a story."  With the "my sweetie" title, maybe it would have been cool to see you on the horse.  That would be a little hard to capture as a self-portrait, but I think it would have been cool to see your affection for him/her :)<br/> <br/>Anyway... overall a nice job -- hopefully this is the most extensive comment you''ll get during this challenge, or I''ll feel like a goober.  I gave it a 6.  Good luck in the challenge!</td>', 'Hello there! I have tried to make a habit out of leaving a super-extensive comment for "milestone" votes of mine.  Turns out, your shot is the 200,000th vote I have cast at DPC!  So... for what it''s worth, here is my super-extensive comment :) First, the positives.  I can see that you used a flash to brighten up the horse''s face.  That looks like it helped to bring out the detail in the fur a bit.  I wonder what a bigger source of light, like a reflector, would have done here. I like the various colors in here.  The greens stand out nicely behind the horse... and the puffy gray clouds add a touch of contrast to the white clouds in the sky. Overall I think the composition is good... I might have chopped out just a little more of the sky, though. As for nitpicky things... I probably would have cloned out the tiny little bird above his back -- it looks like a dust speck (maybe it is a dust speck!).  I would have been tempted to clone out the hot sot on his forehead, too. I guess my biggest nitpick would be that it''s a little plain, and maybe it doesn''t really "tell a story."  With the "my sweetie" title, maybe it would have been cool to see you on the horse.  That would be a little hard to capture as a self-portrait, but I think it would have been cool to see your affection for him/her :) Anyway... overall a nice job -- hopefully this is the most extensive comment you''ll get during this challenge, or I''ll feel like a goober.  I gave it a 6.  Good luck in the challenge!', '2009-03-12 14:09:32.000000', NULL, 1),
