(5326096, 771829, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is very sweetly rendered, but it''s marred, in my eyes, by a distinct lean to the right. It''s as if you rotated to level the implied horizon of the shoreline and the trees and the lamp posts went off vertical. For what it''s worth, you can "level" shots like this with the skew tool: working from this version, just skew upper left corner to the left and bring the trees into alignment. Or rotate original to align trees and skew down on the right to level the shoreline if you need to; I''m not sure it''s required that the shoreline be pure level, though...</td>', 'This is very sweetly rendered, but it''s marred, in my eyes, by a distinct lean to the right. It''s as if you rotated to level the implied horizon of the shoreline and the trees and the lamp posts went off vertical. For what it''s worth, you can "level" shots like this with the skew tool: working from this version, just skew upper left corner to the left and bring the trees into alignment. Or rotate original to align trees and skew down on the right to level the shoreline if you need to; I''m not sure it''s required that the shoreline be pure level, though...', '2009-03-12 17:20:35.000000', NULL, 1),
