(5326236, 771124, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is strange... Image and processing are in general first-rate, but there''s a distinct sense of "lean" to it. I''m aware the light itself is essentially squared up, but the walkway pylons seem skewed. Not only that, the jetty seems artificially horizontal, if you catch my drift? <br/> <br/>I''d be tempted to try skewing left to square the pylons then skewing down to make the jetty just a bit of a diagonal; I think that would feel more natural to me...<br/> <br/>Something like this, maybe, though the actual horizon seems a tad off now, but that''s fixable..<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=773015" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/773015.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/773015.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/773015.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This is strange... Image and processing are in general first-rate, but there''s a distinct sense of "lean" to it. I''m aware the light itself is essentially squared up, but the walkway pylons seem skewed. Not only that, the jetty seems artificially horizontal, if you catch my drift?  I''d be tempted to try skewing left to square the pylons then skewing down to make the jetty just a bit of a diagonal; I think that would feel more natural to me... Something like this, maybe, though the actual horizon seems a tad off now, but that''s fixable.. ', '2009-03-12 17:32:38.000000', NULL, 1),
