(5330225, 772519, 2612, '<td valign="top">Why is it that my landscapes featuring drift wood turn out like crap and yours look like this? It just doesn''t seem fair.<br/> <br/>I really like the layering of this. The driftwood in the foreground is nice, but what makes this great is that you allowed the highlight on the water, in the middle of the frame, draw the eyes back and then the highlights in the mountains carry on from there. Wonderful shot.</td>', 'Why is it that my landscapes featuring drift wood turn out like crap and yours look like this? It just doesn''t seem fair. I really like the layering of this. The driftwood in the foreground is nice, but what makes this great is that you allowed the highlight on the water, in the middle of the frame, draw the eyes back and then the highlights in the mountains carry on from there. Wonderful shot.', '2009-03-12 23:23:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5330226, 770537, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. This is just about as -close- as I want to get to a florida gator...plus I get to enjoy it from the safety of my computer screen:-) I remember seeing this is the portfolio and admiring the dedication to get the shot but shaking my head at the same time...Love the details I see from the bumpy textures of the skin to the beady eye that just waits for us to get closer before it clamps down for a nice tasty morsel. Love how we can see some the details of the submerged body. The water was really nice and clear as glass for you not only can see more details on this gator but you have some really nice reflections of the sunset sky. Composition is wonderful too with this alligator taking front and center stage so that we really get up close and personal with it.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. This is just about as -close- as I want to get to a florida gator...plus I get to enjoy it from the safety of my computer screen:-) I remember seeing this is the portfolio and admiring the dedication to get the shot but shaking my head at the same time...Love the details I see from the bumpy textures of the skin to the beady eye that just waits for us to get closer before it clamps down for a nice tasty morsel. Love how we can see some the details of the submerged body. The water was really nice and clear as glass for you not only can see more details on this gator but you have some really nice reflections of the sunset sky. Composition is wonderful too with this alligator taking front and center stage so that we really get up close and personal with it.', '2009-03-12 23:24:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5330227, 771218, 2615, '<td valign="top">Wow! Great shot! Subject, composition, fantastic!</td>', 'Wow! Great shot! Subject, composition, fantastic!', '2009-03-12 23:24:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5330228, 770508, 53814, '<td valign="top">A fantastic illusion. Subtler than a Banksy (at least the ones I''ve seen), but with more substance. If the photographer is also the artist, then this must be <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=74588" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">cutout</a>. If not, then this is still a great find, well seen and captured. I''ll score this a 10, though I doubt if I''ll vote on 20%, so my vote probably won''t count. Anyway, I''m guessing you don''t care much about scores.</td>', 'A fantastic illusion. Subtler than a Banksy (at least the ones I''ve seen), but with more substance. If the photographer is also the artist, then this must be  cutout. If not, then this is still a great find, well seen and captured. I''ll score this a 10, though I doubt if I''ll vote on 20%, so my vote probably won''t count. Anyway, I''m guessing you don''t care much about scores.', '2009-03-12 23:24:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5330229, 771174, 18197, '<td valign="top">I really like cityscapes and this is no exception. Only one suggestion ... it feels like it''s tilting to the right ... maybe an optical illusion but if it were me, I''d level it. Then again, I''m a nut about accidental tilt, so don''t sweat it.</td>', 'I really like cityscapes and this is no exception. Only one suggestion ... it feels like it''s tilting to the right ... maybe an optical illusion but if it were me, I''d level it. Then again, I''m a nut about accidental tilt, so don''t sweat it.', '2009-03-12 23:24:47.000000', NULL, 1),
