(5331197, 772402, 28710, '<td valign="top">Great pic of the flower and good choice for colors. It''s pretty obvious that you put significant thought and effort into the lighting on this one and it has been done very effectively.<br/> <br/>A bit of blur on the BG area would have been good I think. This would have been easy to do by using one of the color channels as a layer mask.<br/> <br/>I don''t know if it''s intentional, but there a bit of ''blotchiness'' in the overall tone of greens in the BG which help give it a more natural look as if it were a strongly out of focus background area. <br/> <br/>Also, the tone of the greens in the BG change from warm to cool, which is a bit odd. Might have been worth just a tiny bit more tweaking to equalize that. Maybe not.<br/> <br/>I don''t think the border helps anything here. It would have been preferable to have a larger view of the flower. It certainly seems that you have enough detail to manage that.</td>', 'Great pic of the flower and good choice for colors. It''s pretty obvious that you put significant thought and effort into the lighting on this one and it has been done very effectively. A bit of blur on the BG area would have been good I think. This would have been easy to do by using one of the color channels as a layer mask. I don''t know if it''s intentional, but there a bit of ''blotchiness'' in the overall tone of greens in the BG which help give it a more natural look as if it were a strongly out of focus background area.  Also, the tone of the greens in the BG change from warm to cool, which is a bit odd. Might have been worth just a tiny bit more tweaking to equalize that. Maybe not. I don''t think the border helps anything here. It would have been preferable to have a larger view of the flower. It certainly seems that you have enough detail to manage that.', '2009-03-13 01:54:21.000000', NULL, 1),
