(5335157, 771971, 30861, '<td valign="top">Breaking all the rules, aren''t ya? Nothing in the picture is sharp except a few strands of hair and the immediate curve of her shoulder, and the face is almost entirely hidden. The interesting thing is just how much we *can* make out about her despite the softness; that she is, for instance, of Asian extraction, that she *does* seem sad or at least introspective, and even, possibly, that she''s normally somewhat of an extrovert, given the cut of her clothing.<br/> <br/>Anyhow, I digress... It works very well, IMO, and you get a bump from the screening group from me.</td>', 'Breaking all the rules, aren''t ya? Nothing in the picture is sharp except a few strands of hair and the immediate curve of her shoulder, and the face is almost entirely hidden. The interesting thing is just how much we *can* make out about her despite the softness; that she is, for instance, of Asian extraction, that she *does* seem sad or at least introspective, and even, possibly, that she''s normally somewhat of an extrovert, given the cut of her clothing. Anyhow, I digress... It works very well, IMO, and you get a bump from the screening group from me.', '2009-03-13 10:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
