(5335263, 771314, 30861, '<td valign="top">Excellent. Really.... Back to re-evaluate the screening group and bumping you up. <br/> <br/>I''m finding this image weird, I really am. I stare closely at the signage and I can make out that there''s a café inside, and a chapel, and a box office, and a shop, and, of all things, "brass rubbings"?<br/> <br/>Elementary deduction tells me this is probably in England, and it may very well be an entrance into a part of the British Museum? See how hard you''re making me work? Off to google now...<br/> <br/>Nawp, found it :-) It''s the London Brass Rubbing Centre (the Crypt) at St. Martin''s-in-the-Field. Proud of me?<br/> <br/>Anyhow, the image is subtle and in-your-face all at the same time, and I find myself liking it more and more.</td>', 'Excellent. Really.... Back to re-evaluate the screening group and bumping you up.  I''m finding this image weird, I really am. I stare closely at the signage and I can make out that there''s a café inside, and a chapel, and a box office, and a shop, and, of all things, "brass rubbings"? Elementary deduction tells me this is probably in England, and it may very well be an entrance into a part of the British Museum? See how hard you''re making me work? Off to google now... Nawp, found it :-) It''s the London Brass Rubbing Centre (the Crypt) at St. Martin''s-in-the-Field. Proud of me? Anyhow, the image is subtle and in-your-face all at the same time, and I find myself liking it more and more.', '2009-03-13 11:11:32.000000', NULL, 1),
