(5339133, 770582, 101702, '<td valign="top">I''m hoping to leave comments on as many photo''s in this challenge as possible... out of (currently) 1124 images, I gave 31 of them a 9. Your image was one of those 31. <br/> <br/>There are a couple of panoramic shots in this challenge, but yours jumped out at me much more than the others. The lighting and colours are exquisite, with a nice brooding sky. It really makes Atlanta look beautiful (I have no idea whether it actually is!). I''m guessing you were limited by the horizontal dimension allowed for this challenge, I''d love to see this in it''s full size/resolution. <br/> <br/>Good luck for a strong finish in this challenge.</td>', 'I''m hoping to leave comments on as many photo''s in this challenge as possible... out of (currently) 1124 images, I gave 31 of them a 9. Your image was one of those 31.  There are a couple of panoramic shots in this challenge, but yours jumped out at me much more than the others. The lighting and colours are exquisite, with a nice brooding sky. It really makes Atlanta look beautiful (I have no idea whether it actually is!). I''m guessing you were limited by the horizontal dimension allowed for this challenge, I''d love to see this in it''s full size/resolution.  Good luck for a strong finish in this challenge.', '2009-03-13 15:22:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5339134, 771926, 101702, '<td valign="top">I''m hoping to leave comments on as many photo''s in this challenge as possible... out of (currently) 1124 images, I gave 31 of them a 9. Your image was one of those 31. <br/> <br/>There are lots of sea/sunset/pier pictures in this challenge, but yours is one of my favourites. I like the way the long exposure has fogged the water, giving the reflections of the sky a very muted appearance. Just enough foreground to tie the image together wonderfully with an extra splash of colour.<br/> <br/>Good luck for a strong finish in this challenge.</td>', 'I''m hoping to leave comments on as many photo''s in this challenge as possible... out of (currently) 1124 images, I gave 31 of them a 9. Your image was one of those 31.  There are lots of sea/sunset/pier pictures in this challenge, but yours is one of my favourites. I like the way the long exposure has fogged the water, giving the reflections of the sky a very muted appearance. Just enough foreground to tie the image together wonderfully with an extra splash of colour. Good luck for a strong finish in this challenge.', '2009-03-13 15:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
