(5339221, 770477, 52500, '<td valign="top">I figured as soon as this popped up that it was <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=656" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gordon</a>''s.  I just saw that you posted a 3.something in the scores thread, so now I''m sure it''s yours.  It''s strange how people let their expectations determine whether or not they like something.  "A photo <i>should </i>have something in focus, so this is bad."  I wonder how many "There''s nothing in focus." comments you''re getting!  Personally, I love the composition and soothing warm tones.  I also enjoy images that are simultaneously abstract yet recognizable. Your title got me wondering, too, and I learned some things I didn''t know before.  I had you at a 7, but I''m bumping you to an 8 on my second pass.</td>', 'I figured as soon as this popped up that it was  Gordon''s.  I just saw that you posted a 3.something in the scores thread, so now I''m sure it''s yours.  It''s strange how people let their expectations determine whether or not they like something.  "A photo should have something in focus, so this is bad."  I wonder how many "There''s nothing in focus." comments you''re getting!  Personally, I love the composition and soothing warm tones.  I also enjoy images that are simultaneously abstract yet recognizable. Your title got me wondering, too, and I learned some things I didn''t know before.  I had you at a 7, but I''m bumping you to an 8 on my second pass.', '2009-03-13 15:30:28.000000', NULL, 1),
