(5348816, 772487, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to leave comments. The expression, the pose, and the title really made me chuckle. Of course it would have been better had it been a real mouse BUT that would have been an exercise is frustration:-) The thing that really makes this photo is the cat''s expression. He/she really looks lost &amp; confused as he/she stares deeply into our eyes asking ''where *IS* that mouse I was chasing''. Color tones and details are good, but lighting (I know, picky picky right?:-) )could have been a bit better to illuminate the far right portion of the cat and the toy mouse so that we see it more (especially the eye).</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to leave comments. The expression, the pose, and the title really made me chuckle. Of course it would have been better had it been a real mouse BUT that would have been an exercise is frustration:-) The thing that really makes this photo is the cat''s expression. He/she really looks lost & confused as he/she stares deeply into our eyes asking ''where *IS* that mouse I was chasing''. Color tones and details are good, but lighting (I know, picky picky right?:-) )could have been a bit better to illuminate the far right portion of the cat and the toy mouse so that we see it more (especially the eye).', '2009-03-14 12:05:49.000000', NULL, 1),
