(5356982, 770257, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. HOLY MOLY! I am floored with the level of details I see on the great macro. I can clearly see the pollen clustered all over this bee''s legs and body. The detail does not stop there but I see all the hairs on the legs to the bumpy texture around it''s compound eyes. Love the title too which is a clever play on the visual of the bee (B) holding onto the flower petal (/) in the shot itself. Ah, nuts, here comes the critique, everybody has got to be a critic right;-) ...My only critique is that I wished we were able to see more of the full body of the bee complete with the wings in the composition. That way we can appreciate all the intricate and interesting detail of this insect.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. HOLY MOLY! I am floored with the level of details I see on the great macro. I can clearly see the pollen clustered all over this bee''s legs and body. The detail does not stop there but I see all the hairs on the legs to the bumpy texture around it''s compound eyes. Love the title too which is a clever play on the visual of the bee (B) holding onto the flower petal (/) in the shot itself. Ah, nuts, here comes the critique, everybody has got to be a critic right;-) ...My only critique is that I wished we were able to see more of the full body of the bee complete with the wings in the composition. That way we can appreciate all the intricate and interesting detail of this insect.', '2009-03-15 00:22:36.000000', NULL, 1),
