(5367631, 770247, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. Wonderful shot of this remote beachside pier!! Love how you composed the shot such that the boardwalk extrudes out from the bottom left corner to travel to the center portion where we see the pier rest area, perhaps a loading dock and a boat. That adds tremendous visual appeal for it give the eye a natural path to travel on; a leading line that leads off to the vanishing point off into the horizon. Colors are great too with some nice cloud patterns &amp; color and nice silvery blue gleams upon the water.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to leave comments now. Wonderful shot of this remote beachside pier!! Love how you composed the shot such that the boardwalk extrudes out from the bottom left corner to travel to the center portion where we see the pier rest area, perhaps a loading dock and a boat. That adds tremendous visual appeal for it give the eye a natural path to travel on; a leading line that leads off to the vanishing point off into the horizon. Colors are great too with some nice cloud patterns & color and nice silvery blue gleams upon the water.', '2009-03-15 20:31:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5367634, 772069, 103229, '<td valign="top">like the emotion, but something seems to be missing maybe a little more photoshop would help</td>', 'like the emotion, but something seems to be missing maybe a little more photoshop would help', '2009-03-15 20:31:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5367637, 770629, 18197, '<td valign="top">We''ve seen an aweful lot of guitars over the years but this is about the best I''ve ever seen. Black background was inspired. The form and shape of the guitar are pleasing. The color is subtly managed. DOF is powerful. Among best in class.</td>', 'We''ve seen an aweful lot of guitars over the years but this is about the best I''ve ever seen. Black background was inspired. The form and shape of the guitar are pleasing. The color is subtly managed. DOF is powerful. Among best in class.', '2009-03-15 20:31:36.000000', NULL, 1),
