(5369905, 770508, 30861, '<td valign="top">Ah, lovely. What an absolutely *strange* echoing of both classes of element in the dark rectangle. Has me scratching my head trying to figure out just where the dark plane is located relative to the concrete wall, since we''re *seeing* (apparently) the same wall THROUGH its apertures, yet it seems to be a penetration OF the wall. Bizarro. Bumping on second pass.</td>', 'Ah, lovely. What an absolutely *strange* echoing of both classes of element in the dark rectangle. Has me scratching my head trying to figure out just where the dark plane is located relative to the concrete wall, since we''re *seeing* (apparently) the same wall THROUGH its apertures, yet it seems to be a penetration OF the wall. Bizarro. Bumping on second pass.', '2009-03-15 23:47:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5369906, 770248, 79955, '<td valign="top">Not too hot with the composition</td>', 'Not too hot with the composition', '2009-03-15 23:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5369907, 771981, 54645, '<td valign="top">Wonderful composition. The cloud capping the tree is just perfect. I love the way the clouds lead me to that tiny hovel of home. Very well done.8</td>', 'Wonderful composition. The cloud capping the tree is just perfect. I love the way the clouds lead me to that tiny hovel of home. Very well done.8', '2009-03-15 23:47:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5369908, 770981, 37845, '<td valign="top">I love cottages. Great shot of a nice relaxing scene.</td>', 'I love cottages. Great shot of a nice relaxing scene.', '2009-03-15 23:47:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5369910, 771978, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is just ephemeral. I wonder how it''s doing? It''s so understated it''s probably being overlooked, but I like it very much. The quality of the water, that''s SUCH a hard thing to capture, to make it soft instead of harsh. But what really sets this image into a special class is the drop-off to the right. If it were just a straightish landline, left to right, then it''s a nice shot but nothing more. But something about that dropoff is just SO compelling; no wonder the figures are headed that way :-) Good luck with this one!</td>', 'This is just ephemeral. I wonder how it''s doing? It''s so understated it''s probably being overlooked, but I like it very much. The quality of the water, that''s SUCH a hard thing to capture, to make it soft instead of harsh. But what really sets this image into a special class is the drop-off to the right. If it were just a straightish landline, left to right, then it''s a nice shot but nothing more. But something about that dropoff is just SO compelling; no wonder the figures are headed that way :-) Good luck with this one!', '2009-03-15 23:47:29.000000', NULL, 1),
