(5387190, 771787, 32011, '<td valign="top">Not voting, just commenting... and the fact that you already know what I think of this image, there''s not really too much point to this comment other than to get me one vote closer to the 100 comments mark (God know''s I''m not going to go for the 100% comment target, that''s just crazy... impossible for that matter if they''re all as long and rambling as this comment).<br/> <br/>In all seriousness though.  An excellent image, and should have been your free study shot last month, but lucky for you, this Gem challenge comes along and you get to use an image you didn''t have the cohones to use in the Feb Free Study for fear of getting another DQ.  I''m rambling again, aren''t I... I''m not even going to get close to 100 comments at this rate... but you know what, I''m enjoying the free style writing exercise this comment has become... I might even try a few <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a> type comments while attempting the 100 comment goal... just to make it interesting, though, my writing abilities are nowhere near those of K10DGuy.<br/> <br/>Back to your photo.  In the words of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=67587" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Conner</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=92512" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">rodfulk</a> before they got blasted for trying to get a 100% comments ribbon with their minimalist, cut-and-paste comments... <b>"Great shot"</b> <br/> <br/>Seriously though... I love the colour variation and the randomness of the light in this shot.  I''m not sure about the light in the base of the glass... that might cost you some points with the voters, as too might the rim of the glass... but too hell with those voters that can''t recognise a brilliant image when they see it.  Excellent image.</td>', 'Not voting, just commenting... and the fact that you already know what I think of this image, there''s not really too much point to this comment other than to get me one vote closer to the 100 comments mark (God know''s I''m not going to go for the 100% comment target, that''s just crazy... impossible for that matter if they''re all as long and rambling as this comment). In all seriousness though.  An excellent image, and should have been your free study shot last month, but lucky for you, this Gem challenge comes along and you get to use an image you didn''t have the cohones to use in the Feb Free Study for fear of getting another DQ.  I''m rambling again, aren''t I... I''m not even going to get close to 100 comments at this rate... but you know what, I''m enjoying the free style writing exercise this comment has become... I might even try a few  K10DGuy type comments while attempting the 100 comment goal... just to make it interesting, though, my writing abilities are nowhere near those of K10DGuy. Back to your photo.  In the words of  Conner and  rodfulk before they got blasted for trying to get a 100% comments ribbon with their minimalist, cut-and-paste comments... "Great shot"  Seriously though... I love the colour variation and the randomness of the light in this shot.  I''m not sure about the light in the base of the glass... that might cost you some points with the voters, as too might the rim of the glass... but too hell with those voters that can''t recognise a brilliant image when they see it.  Excellent image.', '2009-03-17 21:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
