(5388414, 771260, 51001, '<td valign="top">Post-Challenge:  Wow, 60 comments.  Thanks to everyone who took the time to vote, and to provide critique.<br/> <br/>As for questions/suggestions:<br/>- yes, the railroad was a 100% desat + increased contrast.  My intent was to<br/>   emphasize the color in the trees and perhaps contrast "industry vs.<br/>   nature".  Most of the commenters seemed to pick up on this, and IMO it<br/>   has much more impact than the original.<br/>- JPEG artifacts:  b/c of the complexity of the image (gravel, leaves) it didn''t<br/>   compress well, and I had to lower the quality to meet the 200K file size<br/>   limit.  The original looks much better.<br/>- Leading lines:  My intent was symmetry in the image.  Having them lead to<br/>   a steam locomotive would have been better, but, wasn''t available.<br/>- I was on a railroad overpass looking down on the tracks.<br/> <br/>Again, thanks for all the input!<br/></td>', 'Post-Challenge:  Wow, 60 comments.  Thanks to everyone who took the time to vote, and to provide critique. As for questions/suggestions:- yes, the railroad was a 100% desat + increased contrast.  My intent was to   emphasize the color in the trees and perhaps contrast "industry vs.   nature".  Most of the commenters seemed to pick up on this, and IMO it   has much more impact than the original.- JPEG artifacts:  b/c of the complexity of the image (gravel, leaves) it didn''t   compress well, and I had to lower the quality to meet the 200K file size   limit.  The original looks much better.- Leading lines:  My intent was symmetry in the image.  Having them lead to   a steam locomotive would have been better, but, wasn''t available.- I was on a railroad overpass looking down on the tracks. Again, thanks for all the input!', '2009-03-18 02:13:20.000000', NULL, 0),
