(5388880, 772240, 6958, '<td valign="top">This is the Berlin Memorial, a monument to the six million Jews exterminated by the Nazis.<br/>The "Field of Stelea" is made of 2,711 concrete blocks of different heights, structured in a grid pattern.<br/> <br/>I''ve preferred not to mention directly "what it is" because I wanted the picture to be judged for the atmosphere, composition and abstract concept. I didn''t want to gain more <br/>profit from an easy emotional approach.<br/> <br/>However, I''ve left two significant clues: the strange title (yeah Juliahu, remember + berlin at present continuous) and the splash of red on the woman''s shirt. As Cnovack wrote, my attempt was to evoke the little girl of Schindler''s list movie.<br/> <br/>I would thank you all of you, for your precious comments and positive reactions.<br/> <br/>A special one for you, Cnovack, for the time you''ve spent to write the comment and to have really understood this picture''s soul.<br/> <br/>Finally, thanks to the unaware girl captured in my shot (she''s not a model):<br/>Thank you, whoever you are, wherever you are :-D</td>', 'This is the Berlin Memorial, a monument to the six million Jews exterminated by the Nazis.The "Field of Stelea" is made of 2,711 concrete blocks of different heights, structured in a grid pattern. I''ve preferred not to mention directly "what it is" because I wanted the picture to be judged for the atmosphere, composition and abstract concept. I didn''t want to gain more profit from an easy emotional approach. However, I''ve left two significant clues: the strange title (yeah Juliahu, remember + berlin at present continuous) and the splash of red on the woman''s shirt. As Cnovack wrote, my attempt was to evoke the little girl of Schindler''s list movie. I would thank you all of you, for your precious comments and positive reactions. A special one for you, Cnovack, for the time you''ve spent to write the comment and to have really understood this picture''s soul. Finally, thanks to the unaware girl captured in my shot (she''s not a model):Thank you, whoever you are, wherever you are :-D', '2009-03-18 07:19:45.000000', NULL, 0),
