(5389143, 770255, 13207, '<td valign="top">I completely agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=71239" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">MilesW</a> - this was a 10 and a fave for me and I completely expected it to score much closer to the top.</td>', 'I completely agree with  MilesW - this was a 10 and a fave for me and I completely expected it to score much closer to the top.', '2009-03-18 09:27:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389144, 770206, 70128, '<td valign="top">OMG!!! I was SO close to getting my first ribbon! Shame it was going to be a brown one though! LOL<br/> <br/>I really want to thank you all who took the time to rate and even comment on my picture. This if the first time I got so many comments, and I truly appreciate them. To those who were wondering what this was, there is a comment to it, but it was a very simple shot. I knew it was not going to do really well, although I honestly didn''t think it was going to do this bad! I must admit, I keep my monitor rather dark, and I noticed that if I increase its brightness, my picture can be a bit too harsh. It should have been darker. I have to remember from now on that I actually see things darker than they really are! I didn''t clone out the dust, since that was supposed to be the star field!<br/> <br/>I also want to apologize for mispelling my title, it''s "across" not "accross". I had realized that, but I couldn''t change it anymore, and then someone else noticed it too!! LOL Oh well!<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks again for your patience in voting and commenting. There were SO many wonderful shots in this challenge!<br/> <br/>PS: popdeepop, where you just kidding about buying this!??? if you were not, it''s yours, its price is 0.00!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-18 09:38:59.</i></td>', 'OMG!!! I was SO close to getting my first ribbon! Shame it was going to be a brown one though! LOL I really want to thank you all who took the time to rate and even comment on my picture. This if the first time I got so many comments, and I truly appreciate them. To those who were wondering what this was, there is a comment to it, but it was a very simple shot. I knew it was not going to do really well, although I honestly didn''t think it was going to do this bad! I must admit, I keep my monitor rather dark, and I noticed that if I increase its brightness, my picture can be a bit too harsh. It should have been darker. I have to remember from now on that I actually see things darker than they really are! I didn''t clone out the dust, since that was supposed to be the star field! I also want to apologize for mispelling my title, it''s "across" not "accross". I had realized that, but I couldn''t change it anymore, and then someone else noticed it too!! LOL Oh well! Anyway, thanks again for your patience in voting and commenting. There were SO many wonderful shots in this challenge! PS: popdeepop, where you just kidding about buying this!??? if you were not, it''s yours, its price is 0.00!', '2009-03-18 09:27:46.000000', '2009-03-18 09:38:59.000000', 0),
(5389146, 770912, 66193, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one, but if I had, it would''ve been a 9.  I really like the contrasting blue and gold tones, as well as the look from the 30s exposure.  congrats on a beautiful image.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one, but if I had, it would''ve been a 9.  I really like the contrasting blue and gold tones, as well as the look from the 30s exposure.  congrats on a beautiful image.', '2009-03-18 09:28:35.000000', NULL, 0),
