(5389354, 771161, 99263, '<td valign="top">It made me sad to read about your son''s illness. I would have never have guessed he was ill. In my comment I still mentioned that the photo shows a strong characterful face. I hope there is a chance that he can be cured of whatever it is he is suffering from.<br/> I also still thought that this image had a connection to South Africa. I came from there myself.<br/>Ps. Why are you in exile at this time if you don''t mind me asking? The old ways were buried a long time ago although some remnants refuse to die.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-18 11:08:59.</i></td>', 'It made me sad to read about your son''s illness. I would have never have guessed he was ill. In my comment I still mentioned that the photo shows a strong characterful face. I hope there is a chance that he can be cured of whatever it is he is suffering from. I also still thought that this image had a connection to South Africa. I came from there myself.Ps. Why are you in exile at this time if you don''t mind me asking? The old ways were buried a long time ago although some remnants refuse to die.', '2009-03-18 10:57:59.000000', '2009-03-18 11:08:59.000000', 0),
(5389358, 772520, 68599, '<td valign="top">Wow what a beautiful and emotional photograph you got here. Another one of my faves of the challenge, and of course I expected this to be you. Awesome job. Favoriting another one of your shots. Yet again :)</td>', 'Wow what a beautiful and emotional photograph you got here. Another one of my faves of the challenge, and of course I expected this to be you. Awesome job. Favoriting another one of your shots. Yet again :)', '2009-03-18 10:59:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389360, 770477, 656, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> Great work, Gordon. I had suspected this might be yours. It finished about as bad as one wo0uld expect, I guess, and it''s a pity, but heck y''all knew that going in, right? Lovely image regardless. I''m one of your 9''s. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yup - I''m not too surprised. Lots of positive comments. Lots of interesting comments too. The vote spread is quite different to the company it is keeping down here at the end.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-18 11:01:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: Great work, Gordon. I had suspected this might be yours. It finished about as bad as one wo0uld expect, I guess, and it''s a pity, but heck y''all knew that going in, right? Lovely image regardless. I''m one of your 9''s.   Yup - I''m not too surprised. Lots of positive comments. Lots of interesting comments too. The vote spread is quite different to the company it is keeping down here at the end.', '2009-03-18 10:59:56.000000', '2009-03-18 11:01:21.000000', 0),
(5389364, 771367, 72929, '<td valign="top">Much better than any pic I''ve taken of Watkins glen. The lighting is always tricky in this part of the gorge. Did you do an HDR for this image? (I''m from Rochester so I''ve been there before). Curious to see if you took any of Taughannock falls as well.</td>', 'Much better than any pic I''ve taken of Watkins glen. The lighting is always tricky in this part of the gorge. Did you do an HDR for this image? (I''m from Rochester so I''ve been there before). Curious to see if you took any of Taughannock falls as well.', '2009-03-18 11:02:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389366, 770181, 34101, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments everyone!</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments everyone!', '2009-03-18 11:03:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389373, 770477, 61651, '<td valign="top">Unbelievable, that score.  For what it''s worth, I gave you a 10.  More people should know that defocusing can be a deliberate artistic choice, and your photo, and more importantly your inclusion of the photo in a "gem" challenge, teaches us this.</td>', 'Unbelievable, that score.  For what it''s worth, I gave you a 10.  More people should know that defocusing can be a deliberate artistic choice, and your photo, and more importantly your inclusion of the photo in a "gem" challenge, teaches us this.', '2009-03-18 11:08:28.000000', NULL, 0),
