(5389507, 772233, 11793, '<td valign="top">with a photo of this nature - you''re bound to get an average score.  that doesn''t mean it''s an average photo though.  more that you''ve folks looking at it from the extreme ends of the scale.  sometimes the votes aren''t given based on the quality of the photo, but on how it appeals to the viewer.<br/> <br/>had this been entered in a black on black challenge ( or similarly themed ) it would likely have gotten a much higher score...<br/> <br/>well done !  good work with the metering and holding the highlights.<br/> <br/>my nit pick - the orangish area on the viewers left ( subject right ) side of the head.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-03-18 12:05:00.</i></td>', 'with a photo of this nature - you''re bound to get an average score.  that doesn''t mean it''s an average photo though.  more that you''ve folks looking at it from the extreme ends of the scale.  sometimes the votes aren''t given based on the quality of the photo, but on how it appeals to the viewer. had this been entered in a black on black challenge ( or similarly themed ) it would likely have gotten a much higher score... well done !  good work with the metering and holding the highlights. my nit pick - the orangish area on the viewers left ( subject right ) side of the head.', '2009-03-18 12:03:19.000000', '2009-03-18 12:05:00.000000', 0),
(5389508, 772550, 80096, '<td valign="top">Definitely one of the best of challenge!!!</td>', 'Definitely one of the best of challenge!!!', '2009-03-18 12:03:49.000000', NULL, 0),
