(5389782, 770523, 66494, '<td valign="top">Yeah, I do think this GEM was way underrated. 8 from me. I love the lines, the people really set it off well too.</td>', 'Yeah, I do think this GEM was way underrated. 8 from me. I love the lines, the people really set it off well too.', '2009-03-18 13:43:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389787, 771049, 68504, '<td valign="top">Recognized as yours when previewing entries. Several oscillations keep the viewer suspended or aloft in contemplating form and substance.  Not just the oscillation caused by the wibbly storm window, but the frames within frames, the rectilinear forms within the building facade, and most sweetly mr pussycat backgrounded by and looking at greenery (and possibly sculptures of his master''s race - whitish forms look like faces to me).  One shot. And yet the photo is deceptively quiet.</td>', 'Recognized as yours when previewing entries. Several oscillations keep the viewer suspended or aloft in contemplating form and substance.  Not just the oscillation caused by the wibbly storm window, but the frames within frames, the rectilinear forms within the building facade, and most sweetly mr pussycat backgrounded by and looking at greenery (and possibly sculptures of his master''s race - whitish forms look like faces to me).  One shot. And yet the photo is deceptively quiet.', '2009-03-18 13:47:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389788, 772132, 38162, '<td valign="top">call me a conspiracy nut, but I also detect an anti-NYC bias here.  top of the rock is great place to watch sunsets and really feel the power of midtown far above I(most of) the damn tourists. this is a fine job of raw processing.  this would be trite and boring without your heavy hand in processing.  it would just be a snap, not art.  super job.</td>', 'call me a conspiracy nut, but I also detect an anti-NYC bias here.  top of the rock is great place to watch sunsets and really feel the power of midtown far above I(most of) the damn tourists. this is a fine job of raw processing.  this would be trite and boring without your heavy hand in processing.  it would just be a snap, not art.  super job.', '2009-03-18 13:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389790, 772233, 39343, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, everyone!  I would be interested to hear from folks who voted low - and more than just, "It''s too dark."<br/> <br/>It''s not too dark, it exactly the way I, as the artist, intended it.  I realize that it will vary quite a bit depending on monitor calibration, but I have seen it on a professionally calibrated monitor at a photo lab, and it looks exactly as I intended it.<br/> <br/>I certainly realize that it doesn''t appeal to everyone, but that is the point of art, isn''t it?<br/> <br/>And thanks to the three folks who marked this as a favorite!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, everyone!  I would be interested to hear from folks who voted low - and more than just, "It''s too dark." It''s not too dark, it exactly the way I, as the artist, intended it.  I realize that it will vary quite a bit depending on monitor calibration, but I have seen it on a professionally calibrated monitor at a photo lab, and it looks exactly as I intended it. I certainly realize that it doesn''t appeal to everyone, but that is the point of art, isn''t it? And thanks to the three folks who marked this as a favorite!', '2009-03-18 13:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
