(5389815, 772314, 68504, '<td valign="top">This definitely stood out in my brief previewing.  For me it references old ikons and the more modern pieta by Michelangelo.</td>', 'This definitely stood out in my brief previewing.  For me it references old ikons and the more modern pieta by Michelangelo.', '2009-03-18 14:03:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389816, 772132, 61961, '<td valign="top">Neil, for me this had several strikes against it.  First, I felt inundated by sunsets in this challenge, so this suffered in comparison.  Second, if my score is hovering between two numbers, and I see a letterbox frame, I''ll probably go with the lower number, because I think a letterbox frame adds a quality that isn''t inherent to the photo.  (I realize that may be unfair, but it''s my own personal pet peeve lately).  Most important, though, as a result of processing I thought this ended up sort of "muddy."  I agree with Ken that the print version looks more realistic and may I add sharper.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe:</b></div><hr/><i> call me a conspiracy nut, but I also detect an anti-NYC bias here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Oh yeah, there''s that, too.  I *know* that''s why my entry bombed. ;-)</td>', 'Neil, for me this had several strikes against it.  First, I felt inundated by sunsets in this challenge, so this suffered in comparison.  Second, if my score is hovering between two numbers, and I see a letterbox frame, I''ll probably go with the lower number, because I think a letterbox frame adds a quality that isn''t inherent to the photo.  (I realize that may be unfair, but it''s my own personal pet peeve lately).  Most important, though, as a result of processing I thought this ended up sort of "muddy."  I agree with Ken that the print version looks more realistic and may I add sharper. Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe: call me a conspiracy nut, but I also detect an anti-NYC bias here.  Oh yeah, there''s that, too.  I *know* that''s why my entry bombed. ;-)', '2009-03-18 14:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389819, 772239, 33535, '<td valign="top">i love how you can even see the slight blur of the ball. nice shot!</td>', 'i love how you can even see the slight blur of the ball. nice shot!', '2009-03-18 14:06:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389820, 771681, 63244, '<td valign="top">Love the minimalism of this shot!!<br/>Very underrated.</td>', 'Love the minimalism of this shot!!Very underrated.', '2009-03-18 14:07:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389821, 772535, 30982, '<td valign="top">''Tis always good to see loved ones through they eyes of those that love them.  She really is a beautiful woman - you did her justice!  But by all means, keep shooting her.  :-)</td>', '''Tis always good to see loved ones through they eyes of those that love them.  She really is a beautiful woman - you did her justice!  But by all means, keep shooting her.  :-)', '2009-03-18 14:08:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389824, 772765, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nuzzer:</b></div><hr/><i>I may be wrong and perhaps you do have more of a story to your shot but the fact is that it doesn''t come across to the viewer.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s funny, considering how very, very few shots tell a story in this challenge... and this is one of them.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nuzzer:I may be wrong and perhaps you do have more of a story to your shot but the fact is that it doesn''t come across to the viewer.  That''s funny, considering how very, very few shots tell a story in this challenge... and this is one of them.', '2009-03-18 14:08:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5389828, 770170, 5112, '<td valign="top">Excellent landscape, I so like the little tanker in the way back!  It gives it a touch of human, that works really nicely in this case.  I think this was one of the best landscapes entered to the challenge.</td>', 'Excellent landscape, I so like the little tanker in the way back!  It gives it a touch of human, that works really nicely in this case.  I think this was one of the best landscapes entered to the challenge.', '2009-03-18 14:10:46.000000', NULL, 0),
