(5390274, 771322, 67237, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by cytoxan:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on winning the best of the best. I have a question though. Not living around (or evenly remotely close to) any mountain ranges brings a question to my mind. How are those rocks stacked up like that? Seems like they were placed there by man. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>the answer is in the photographer''s comments:<br/> <br/>"The cairn has been placed to guide trekkers and is actually smaller than it appears  the top of it reaches ones head."</td>', 'Originally posted by cytoxan: Congrats on winning the best of the best. I have a question though. Not living around (or evenly remotely close to) any mountain ranges brings a question to my mind. How are those rocks stacked up like that? Seems like they were placed there by man.   the answer is in the photographer''s comments: "The cairn has been placed to guide trekkers and is actually smaller than it appears  the top of it reaches ones head."', '2009-03-18 17:55:56.000000', NULL, 0),
