(5390315, 772558, 63503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by the99:</b></div><hr/><i> tu as fais un trés bon travail avec cette image, comme toujours.  Elle aurais dû être meilleur placée, mais surement les ânes, ils n ''ont pas aidés le suffisant. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Un poco errada la redaccion en frances pero estoy totalmente de acuerdo con el mensaje. Great picture bro, deserved a first page showing.</td>', 'Originally posted by the99: tu as fais un trés bon travail avec cette image, comme toujours.  Elle aurais dû être meilleur placée, mais surement les ânes, ils n ''ont pas aidés le suffisant.   Un poco errada la redaccion en frances pero estoy totalmente de acuerdo con el mensaje. Great picture bro, deserved a first page showing.', '2009-03-18 18:12:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5390349, 770563, 36914, '<td valign="top">What this is is a light, the shade is the black square with a blue, glass insert, the bulb was a halogen light, with a cube cage around it, the lines did not really show when the light was on but shadowed when shot with the camera.  <br/>The light fixture was at the end of a hallway.<br/>Post processing was align, and crop. <br/>The illusion was that if you moved your head the blue square acted like it was floating around and the center light circle played tricks like expanding and contracting. <br/>If you really saw the light fixture in its area you would never really know that the lines were there until you took the picture.   I shot it because I just wanted the little black square with the blue center piece.<br/></td>', 'What this is is a light, the shade is the black square with a blue, glass insert, the bulb was a halogen light, with a cube cage around it, the lines did not really show when the light was on but shadowed when shot with the camera.  The light fixture was at the end of a hallway.Post processing was align, and crop. The illusion was that if you moved your head the blue square acted like it was floating around and the center light circle played tricks like expanding and contracting. If you really saw the light fixture in its area you would never really know that the lines were there until you took the picture.   I shot it because I just wanted the little black square with the blue center piece.', '2009-03-18 18:28:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5390355, 772313, 7778, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i>...you might still comment anyway I suppose. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, no. I much prefer the question marks you left here to anything I could say.  :-)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by ubique:...you might still comment anyway I suppose.   Well, no. I much prefer the question marks you left here to anything I could say.  :-) ', '2009-03-18 18:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
