(5391189, 771822, 10275, '<td valign="top">Oh, I so knew this was you! You are a "signature" portrait artist. I would recognize your photos anywhere. I love them here, I love them on pBase. I am your long-time secret "stalker" :-)) The colours are so incredible in all of your images. This one just totally pops.</td>', 'Oh, I so knew this was you! You are a "signature" portrait artist. I would recognize your photos anywhere. I love them here, I love them on pBase. I am your long-time secret "stalker" :-)) The colours are so incredible in all of your images. This one just totally pops.', '2009-03-19 03:31:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391190, 771915, 34459, '<td valign="top">Thanks very much everyone for all the comments; much appreciated, some very lovely ones which gave me far more joy than my final score...<br/> <br/>I had hoped this shot would do better than it did but the 5.7/5.8 seemed to stick so I guessed it wouldn''t be top 10 ! Would like to know why so many 3''s &amp; 4''s... perhaps you all thought it was a snap through an aquarium glass or something. Well, as these chaps were 5 metres across, it would have been one hell of an aquarium ! And to the commenter who said the sand was a little featureless, well I''m sorry, but when you''ve sat on the sea bed for best part of an hour waiting for these guys to appear, there''s not an awful lot you can do about that...<br/> <br/>Difficult with so many images to judge, but still disappointing to see some rather more ''ordinary'' pics rated higher. Ah well, such is DPC !</td>', 'Thanks very much everyone for all the comments; much appreciated, some very lovely ones which gave me far more joy than my final score... I had hoped this shot would do better than it did but the 5.7/5.8 seemed to stick so I guessed it wouldn''t be top 10 ! Would like to know why so many 3''s & 4''s... perhaps you all thought it was a snap through an aquarium glass or something. Well, as these chaps were 5 metres across, it would have been one hell of an aquarium ! And to the commenter who said the sand was a little featureless, well I''m sorry, but when you''ve sat on the sea bed for best part of an hour waiting for these guys to appear, there''s not an awful lot you can do about that... Difficult with so many images to judge, but still disappointing to see some rather more ''ordinary'' pics rated higher. Ah well, such is DPC !', '2009-03-19 03:32:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391193, 772163, 10275, '<td valign="top">I don''t get it. Why was this disqualified? It doesn''t look altered. The light is absolutely stunning, so are the animals. This is an incredible photo. You should be proud of it. Forget ribbons, this is a winner in many ways.</td>', 'I don''t get it. Why was this disqualified? It doesn''t look altered. The light is absolutely stunning, so are the animals. This is an incredible photo. You should be proud of it. Forget ribbons, this is a winner in many ways.', '2009-03-19 03:37:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391195, 771734, 8860, '<td valign="top">Lovely catch! Not your typical owl shot for sure - very memorable.</td>', 'Lovely catch! Not your typical owl shot for sure - very memorable.', '2009-03-19 03:39:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391214, 770406, 21540, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much for all the comments.  Many of you talked about some artifacts and a line in the picture.  Something happened in the upload and the picture got corrupted.  It was stupid of me not to look better at the picture after I uploaded.  You can see a better version of it on my Flickr.  Here is a direct link <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/ingvargud/3272919102/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.flickr.com/photos/ingvargud/3272919102/</a> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//farm4.static.flickr.com/3359/3272919102_0c0a782076_o.jpg'', strrpos(''//farm4.static.flickr.com/3359/3272919102_0c0a782076_o.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//farm4.static.flickr.com/3359/3272919102_0c0a782076_o.jpg"/></td>', 'Thank you all very much for all the comments.  Many of you talked about some artifacts and a line in the picture.  Something happened in the upload and the picture got corrupted.  It was stupid of me not to look better at the picture after I uploaded.  You can see a better version of it on my Flickr.  Here is a direct link //www.flickr.com/photos/ingvargud/3272919102/  ', '2009-03-19 04:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
