(5391724, 772525, 35804, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> a toy plane. sharp and correctly exposed, but maybe the most boring shot in the challenge. I cannot imagine why ypu shot that or what your intention was. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>...says the guy who entered this picture:<br/> <br/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=772303" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1005/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_772303.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1005/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_772303.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1005/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_772303.jpg"/></a>.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: a toy plane. sharp and correctly exposed, but maybe the most boring shot in the challenge. I cannot imagine why ypu shot that or what your intention was.   ...says the guy who entered this picture:  . ', '2009-03-19 12:48:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391738, 770850, 42495, '<td valign="top">This was one of my faves during the challenge.  Take away those ones and twos and this would have scored more higher, where it belongs.  What a sad commentary on DPC.</td>', 'This was one of my faves during the challenge.  Take away those ones and twos and this would have scored more higher, where it belongs.  What a sad commentary on DPC.', '2009-03-19 12:52:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5391750, 772193, 64837, '<td valign="top">I wanted to thank everyone who commented, they were much appreciated, well most of them.  I wanted to respond to one in particular though.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=656229" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Is there no end to the rampant plagiarism in this place?</a> (I guess "Eye to the soul" was getting a little old...) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>First off, considering this was an open date challenge and the photo I used was taken in 2007 and I see yours was taken in 2008... and this is the title I''ve used since it''s been in my portfolio, again since 2007, I''m not exactly sure how I plagiarized you, especially since until you pointed out this link, I''ve never seen the photo in question.<br/> <br/>But going even further, I wondered just how many other "Eye See You" titles are on the site, so I did a little search...<br/> <br/>Here we have one from 2002 <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101</a> <br/>here''s another from 2002 complete with the exclamation mark (like you used) <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101</a> <br/>Oh, what''s this? Another from 2003, again complete with the exclamation mark <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=28672" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=28672</a> <br/> <br/>In all, there were 70 results returned, many using the same name...<br/> <br/>So, I guess that makes you a plagiarist, too, right?<br/> <br/></td>', 'I wanted to thank everyone who commented, they were much appreciated, well most of them.  I wanted to respond to one in particular though. Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: Is there no end to the rampant plagiarism in this place? (I guess "Eye to the soul" was getting a little old...)   First off, considering this was an open date challenge and the photo I used was taken in 2007 and I see yours was taken in 2008... and this is the title I''ve used since it''s been in my portfolio, again since 2007, I''m not exactly sure how I plagiarized you, especially since until you pointed out this link, I''ve never seen the photo in question. But going even further, I wondered just how many other "Eye See You" titles are on the site, so I did a little search... Here we have one from 2002 //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101 here''s another from 2002 complete with the exclamation mark (like you used) //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=8101 Oh, what''s this? Another from 2003, again complete with the exclamation mark //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=28672  In all, there were 70 results returned, many using the same name... So, I guess that makes you a plagiarist, too, right? ', '2009-03-19 12:53:57.000000', NULL, 0),
