(5416915, 771248, 67258, '<td valign="top">They look tasty! The white bowl is very effective, and well placed compositionally.  The lighting does seem just a tad harsh, and my eye gets drawn to the cherry at rear right, which is soft due to the fall off in depth of field.</td>', 'They look tasty! The white bowl is very effective, and well placed compositionally.  The lighting does seem just a tad harsh, and my eye gets drawn to the cherry at rear right, which is soft due to the fall off in depth of field.', '2009-04-03 13:07:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416917, 771863, 67258, '<td valign="top">Commented on this one during voting - I did wonder if it was yours, but was sure you had said you hadn''t entered the challenge! For me it is the perfect group photo - well setup and composed but fun and relaxed at the same time.</td>', 'Commented on this one during voting - I did wonder if it was yours, but was sure you had said you hadn''t entered the challenge! For me it is the perfect group photo - well setup and composed but fun and relaxed at the same time.', '2009-04-03 13:09:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416925, 770968, 67258, '<td valign="top">Good detail on the fly, although the light is perhaps a little on the harsh side.  Pleasingly composed, but what I like best is the softness and colour of the petals!  Bemused my the votes of 1, 2 and 3...</td>', 'Good detail on the fly, although the light is perhaps a little on the harsh side.  Pleasingly composed, but what I like best is the softness and colour of the petals!  Bemused my the votes of 1, 2 and 3...', '2009-04-03 13:14:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416927, 770198, 67258, '<td valign="top">A fun and very well seen composition.  I would be tempted to either clone out, or tone down the white sign (?) in the bacground.</td>', 'A fun and very well seen composition.  I would be tempted to either clone out, or tone down the white sign (?) in the bacground.', '2009-04-03 13:16:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416939, 771649, 67258, '<td valign="top">There looks as though there has been heaps of ''life'' in that face - someone with stories to tell.  The background blur sets of the portrait well, and the graininess adds to the overall effect.</td>', 'There looks as though there has been heaps of ''life'' in that face - someone with stories to tell.  The background blur sets of the portrait well, and the graininess adds to the overall effect.', '2009-04-03 13:19:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416943, 770770, 67258, '<td valign="top">What a character - and you have captured the eccentricity well.  The choice of processing is very clever, with the would-be mayor as one with the statues, or perhaps like an animation character, not quite real!</td>', 'What a character - and you have captured the eccentricity well.  The choice of processing is very clever, with the would-be mayor as one with the statues, or perhaps like an animation character, not quite real!', '2009-04-03 13:22:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416946, 770215, 67258, '<td valign="top">I can see why you love this.  The wonderful dappled light gives the feeling that the photographer is stealing a peak at the bird.  The  colour is so vibrant against the dark background.</td>', 'I can see why you love this.  The wonderful dappled light gives the feeling that the photographer is stealing a peak at the bird.  The  colour is so vibrant against the dark background.', '2009-04-03 13:25:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416948, 771517, 67258, '<td valign="top">I looked at this for some time during voting, but in the end couldn''t decide what I made of it (although I guess a viewer makes of any exhibit what they do...) - on the one hand I liked the juxtaposition of the different elements, even though I didn''t know what they all were, and I liked the over-all aesthetic ''feel'', but on the other it somehow bothered and frustrated me that I didn''t understand what the photographer was trying to communicate.</td>', 'I looked at this for some time during voting, but in the end couldn''t decide what I made of it (although I guess a viewer makes of any exhibit what they do...) - on the one hand I liked the juxtaposition of the different elements, even though I didn''t know what they all were, and I liked the over-all aesthetic ''feel'', but on the other it somehow bothered and frustrated me that I didn''t understand what the photographer was trying to communicate.', '2009-04-03 13:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416957, 772498, 67258, '<td valign="top">I was impressed by this during voting, and remain so now.  It is a really strong study of a mundane, every day object.  You have shown the texture of the metal very well, the composition is strong, and the mono-conversion stronger still.</td>', 'I was impressed by this during voting, and remain so now.  It is a really strong study of a mundane, every day object.  You have shown the texture of the metal very well, the composition is strong, and the mono-conversion stronger still.', '2009-04-03 13:35:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5416962, 772119, 67258, '<td valign="top">I like your choice of photo for the challenge, too.  It is technically well taken with an impressively deep depth of field; I particular like the way the texture and colour of the wood and peeling paintwork is shown.</td>', 'I like your choice of photo for the challenge, too.  It is technically well taken with an impressively deep depth of field; I particular like the way the texture and colour of the wood and peeling paintwork is shown.', '2009-04-03 13:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5419304, 770653, 96534, '<td valign="top">Paul! You have snow - major bonus. And a butterfly bridge! And gorgeous trees! You do NOT live in an ugly place at all! LOL I love this shot, it has a very film noire like feel to it. The only thing that I might have done is to clone out the tracks that look like bike tracks? They detract from the footprints slightly and break the symmetry. IMHO only!</td>', 'Paul! You have snow - major bonus. And a butterfly bridge! And gorgeous trees! You do NOT live in an ugly place at all! LOL I love this shot, it has a very film noire like feel to it. The only thing that I might have done is to clone out the tracks that look like bike tracks? They detract from the footprints slightly and break the symmetry. IMHO only!', '2009-04-05 07:05:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5421024, 772527, 46314, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I can''t understand why this didn''t score higher. Terrific use of the diagonal lines - I like how the shadow parallels the wooden boards. And a really nice sharp silhouette - very intersting use of the lighting. Well done.</td>', 'Great shot. I can''t understand why this didn''t score higher. Terrific use of the diagonal lines - I like how the shadow parallels the wooden boards. And a really nice sharp silhouette - very intersting use of the lighting. Well done.', '2009-04-06 04:18:04.000000', NULL, 0),
