(6663398, 772537, 49018, '<td valign="top">What wonderful things one finds with a little patience, just browsing through old challenges or travelling by train.<br/>I remember this story from Tiziano Terzani, a journalist for Der Spiegel. He was travelling on a russian train, in the middle of the steppe, when a massive armed conflict exploded between two gangs of criminals. The huge fellow Russian passengers he shared compartment with basically picked him up and carried him to an empty wagon which they barred. They spent the long night between vodka and bread, laughing without understanding each other, or perhaps not. The train didn''t slow down a bit, piercing the frozen void of the night. Because a train''s job is to carry life, not to stop for it.<br/>Not quite sure why I write this, trains do carry lot of life, but they also freeze the course of things, give time to look back and forward.<br/>Good work.</td>', 'What wonderful things one finds with a little patience, just browsing through old challenges or travelling by train.I remember this story from Tiziano Terzani, a journalist for Der Spiegel. He was travelling on a russian train, in the middle of the steppe, when a massive armed conflict exploded between two gangs of criminals. The huge fellow Russian passengers he shared compartment with basically picked him up and carried him to an empty wagon which they barred. They spent the long night between vodka and bread, laughing without understanding each other, or perhaps not. The train didn''t slow down a bit, piercing the frozen void of the night. Because a train''s job is to carry life, not to stop for it.Not quite sure why I write this, trains do carry lot of life, but they also freeze the course of things, give time to look back and forward.Good work.', '2012-02-03 19:44:37.000000', NULL, 0),
